  m_Name: HydraulicSteeringSystemData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  engineName: Hydraulic Steering System
  engineDescription: A Hydraulic Steering System is a power-assisted steering mechanism
    that uses pressurized hydraulic fluid to reduce the effort required for steering
    vehicles and heavy machinery. Its main components include the hydraulic pump,
    steering gear, control valve, hydraulic cylinder, fluid reservoir, hoses, and
    steering wheel linkage. During operation, the hydraulic pump supplies pressurized
    fluid to the steering gear, where the control valve directs the fluid to assist
    the movement of the steering mechanism according to the driver's input. Hydraulic
    steering systems are widely used in automobiles, trucks, buses, agricultural
    tractors, construction equipment, and marine vessels. From an engineering perspective,
    understanding hydraulic pressure, steering response, fluid flow, system efficiency,
    leakage prevention, and maintenance is essential for ensuring safe, smooth, and
    reliable steering performance.
  engineCategory: Engineering
